{%- assign p = card_product -%}
{%- comment -%}
  The status is worked out once, as a word (snippets/status), and passed on as a string:
  render only passes a value, not a comparison, so `sold: p.available == false` once badged
  every piece in stock.

  A button cannot sit inside a link, so the card is a div: the picture (a second link to the
  same page, hidden from screen readers and the tab order, as in the bag) with the Quick view
  button over it, then the words as the real link. Quick view opens sections/quick-view in a
  dialog; without JavaScript the button stays hidden and the links do the work.

  Every card photograph is a square crop (plate fill), so a row lines up whatever shape the
  photographs are. A coming-soon piece shows its price (or "Price to come") and "Coming soon"
  with its release, so nobody has to open it to find out. card_sizes: the card's display width.

  Tag a piece photo-to-come when its only photograph is shared with another listing (a pair shot
  together): its card shows the shop's cat instead, so the same photograph never appears on two
  cards. The piece's own page still shows the photograph. Remove the tag once it has its own.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture status -%}{%- render 'status', p: p -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign piece = p.metafields.hikari.piece | default: p.title -%}
{%- assign img_sizes = card_sizes | default: '(max-width: 860px) 50vw, 33vw' -%}
{%- assign card_img = p.featured_image -%}
{%- assign to_come = false -%}
{%- if p.tags contains 'photo-to-come' -%}{%- assign card_img = nil -%}{%- assign to_come = true -%}{%- endif -%}
<div class="card">
  <div class="card-media">
    <a href="{{ p.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- render 'plate', image: card_img, ratio: 1, fill: true, sizes: img_sizes, seed: p.id, tone: tone,
          comp: 'single', alt: p.title, badge: status, mark: to_come -%}
    </a>
    <button type="button" class="qv-btn" data-quick-view="{{ p.url }}" aria-haspopup="dialog"
            aria-label="{{ 'products.quick_view.label' | t: house: p.vendor, piece: piece | escape_once }}">{{ 'products.quick_view.title' | t }}</button>
  </div>
  <a class="card-a" href="{{ p.url }}">
    <div class="cinfo">
      <h3 class="chouse">{{ p.vendor | default: p.title }}</h3>
      <p class="cpiece">{{ piece }}</p>
      <div class="crow">
        <span class="price">
          {%- if status == 'sold' -%}{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}{%- else -%}{%- render 'price', p: p -%}{%- endif -%}
        </span>
        {%- if status == 'soon' -%}
          <span class="when">{{ 'products.badge.coming_soon' | t }} · {% render 'release', p: p %}</span>
        {%- else -%}
          <span class="tag">{%- if p.metafields.hikari.grade %}{{ 'products.spec.grade' | t: grade: p.metafields.hikari.grade }}{% endif -%}
            {%- if p.metafields.hikari.measurements %} · {{ p.metafields.hikari.measurements }}{% endif -%}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </a>
</div>
